Use subdetector-specific VolumeManager to avoid ambiguities.

When looking up a volume by VolumeID from VolumeManager, one needs to be
careful of the possibility of VolumeIDs that are duplicated between
different detector systems.  In that case, one need to first fetch the
subdetector-specific VolumeManager and then do the lookup there.

In ALLEGRO, there are duplicate Volume IDs between the HCal and Si wrapper.
Adjust the code here to work correctly in this case.
